+First, couple the four serotype-specific mouse monoclonal antibodies to Diasorin Luminex MagPlex-C Microspheres: use region B20 for anti-MenA (batch 28022017), B25 for anti-MenC (batch 13072017), B33 for anti-MenW (batch 04052017), and B77 for anti-MenY (batch 23082017). For each coupling reaction, wash 100 µL (1.25 million beads) in water using a protein low-binding 1.5 mL tube. Activate the beads with 80 µL of 100 mM sodium phosphate (pH 6.2), 10 µL of sNHS (50 mg/mL), and 10 µL of EDC (50 mg/mL). Mix by 360° rotation for 20 min at room temperature in the dark. Conjugate each activated bead set with its respective mAb in 500 µL of 50 mM MES buffer (pH 5.0), mixing by 360° rotation for 2 h at room temperature in the dark. Wash twice with 500 µL of 1X PBS / 0.05% Tween-20. Saturate unreacted groups with 500 µL of 1X PBS / 0.05% Tween-20 / 0.2% BSA by rotating for 30 min at room temperature in the dark. Wash twice more with 500 mL of 1X PBS / 0.05% Tween-20, and store in 1000 µL of the same buffer at a final concentration of 1.25 million beads/mL.
 
